%description:
Test connection setup with timestamps: a SYN-ACK whose TSecr this side did
not send gets an RST (RFC 7323, Linux PAWSACTIVEREJECTED). The tester sets
the TSecr of B's SYN-ACK to 5, which lies before A's SYN (TSval 1000). A
sends an RST and stays in SYN_SENT; B returns to LISTEN. A's retransmitted
SYN at t=4 then completes the handshake.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.cli_app.tOpen=1s
*.cli_app.sendScript="6 100"
*.*_tcp.timestampSupport = true
*.tcptester.script="b1 tsecr 5"

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "^\[testing\]\|PAWSACTIVEREJECTED" test.out > test_1.out || true
%contains: test_1.out
[testing]: [1.003 B001] A.1000 < B.2000: A S 250500:250500(0) ack 250001 win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize NOP NOP TS(1002,5)# changing TSecr
[]: SYN-ACK TSecr 5 outside [1000, 1004]: sending RST (PAWSACTIVEREJECTED)
[testing]: [1.005 A002] A.1000 > B.2000: R win 0
[testing]: srv_tcp: SYN_RCVD --> LISTEN  (on RCV_RST)
[testing]: [4.001 A003] A.1000 > B.2000: S 250000:250000(0) win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize NOP NOP TS(4000,0)
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
